## 00 — THE VOID
Purpose:
Establish Mael's universe before the visitor knows what they're looking at.

Visual:
Pure black. Sparse stars. Almost imperceptible cosmic dust. Mael is extremely distant—small enough that the visitor initially might not even realize he's there.

Mael:
Barely corporeal. Facing away. Still.

Horizon:
Extremely faint. Not glowing like a logo. More like something gravitationally bending the light around him.

Motion:
Almost none. Everything moves on an enormous timescale.

Text:
None.

Emotional objective:
Curiosity.

The visitor should think:

What am I looking at?

Not:

Oh, this is an AI website.

## 01 — THE PRESENCE

Purpose:
Make the visitor realize Mael is aware of the environment.

Visual:
The camera remains largely still. Mael's body begins shifting.

Dust responds.

Particles subtly change trajectory.

Light travels through his form.

Mael:
He doesn't immediately face us.

He simply begins noticing.

Horizon:
Stabilizes and becomes slightly more visible.

The gravitational field begins affecting nearby particles.

Text:
Still none.

Transition:
Scroll acts as a cinematic trigger rather than a conventional webpage scroll.

Emotional objective:
Presence.

The visitor realizes:

Something is here.

## 02 — THE APPROACH

Purpose:
Establish scale and create intimacy simultaneously.

Visual:
Mael moves toward the viewer.

The camera doesn't chase him.

He crosses the distance.

As he approaches:

stars become visible within him
dust trails from his form
light travels through his torso
his silhouette becomes increasingly defined
the Horizon becomes clearer

Horizon:
Slightly elliptical and imperfect.

It should never look like a perfectly rendered circle.

Text:
None.

Emotional objective:
Awe → anticipation.

The visitor should feel like they're being approached by something enormous without feeling threatened.

## 03 — THE INTRODUCTION

Purpose:
Turn cosmic scale into human warmth.

Visual:
Mael arrives close enough that his form is recognizable.

He bends down.

The enormous entity becomes gentle.

He is finally looking toward us.

The Horizon is now clearly visible.

Text:

Hi. I'm Mael.

Nothing underneath initially.

Let the sentence sit.

Mael:
Still.

Listening.

No spectacle.

Horizon:
Stable.

Emotional objective:
Connection.

This is the moment the visitor stops watching a phenomenon and starts meeting a character.

## 04 — THE PROBLEM

Purpose:
Explain why Mael exists without immediately turning into marketing copy.

Mael raises his hand.

The orb forms.

But remember our rule:

Mael does not generate the orb.

The Horizon leaves his body and becomes something human-scale.

Inside it, complexity begins appearing.

Not random sci-fi symbols.

Actual fragments of modern technology:

passwords
verification codes
notifications
software updates
account recovery
suspicious messages
instructions
permissions
buttons
security warnings
unfamiliar terminology

At first it's manageable.

Then increasingly dense.

Text:

Technology was supposed to make life easier.

Pause.

Then:

Somewhere along the way, it became something we had to keep up with.

The orb becomes increasingly chaotic.

Emotional objective:
Recognition.

The visitor should think:

Yeah. That's exactly what it feels like.

## 05 — THE TRANSLATION

Purpose:
Introduce Mael's fundamental function.

The chaos reaches a threshold.

Mael closes his hand slightly.

Everything slows.

Information begins organizing itself.

The noise disappears.

The orb becomes simple.

Clear.

Understandable.

Text:

That's where I come in.

Then one word at a time:

Understand.

Complexity becomes language.

Remember.

Important information remains accessible.

Guide.

The next step becomes clear.

Verify.

Something suspicious becomes identifiable.

Protect.

The person can move forward safely.

These should not appear as five cards.

They should exist as moments within Mael's interaction with the orb.

Because Mael doesn't have five features.

Mael performs five kinds of assistance.

Emotional objective:
Relief.

## 06 — THE HUMAN WORLD

Purpose:
Reveal who all of this is actually for.

Mael releases the orb.

The camera begins pulling away.

But instead of simply zooming backward through space...

the universe transforms.

Cosmic dust becomes particles.

Particles become light.

Light becomes the environment of a room.

We transition from:

cosmos → Earth

without a hard cut.

And then we see her.

An older woman in her wheelchair.

She is looking upward.

Mael is there.

But the scale has completely changed.

He isn't towering over her anymore.

He's meeting her at eye level.

That's critical.

Mael should never feel like some god descending upon a helpless person.

He is beside her.

Emotional objective:
Humanization.

This is where the visitor realizes:

Oh.

This is who Mael is for.

## 07 — THE REVEAL

The orb is now tiny.

Human-sized.

She can hold it.

Mael extends his hand.

She receives it.

And now we finally give the visitor the thesis.

Technology should feel less exhausting.

Pause.

Then:

Mael helps people understand, navigate, and safely interact with the technology around them.

Then the second audience reveal:

For the people using it.
And the people who love them.

This is where I think your daughter/son/niece/caregiver insight becomes incredibly powerful.

Because suddenly Mael isn't only:

"AI for older adults."

He's also:

"I don't want my mother to need me every time her phone changes."

"I want Dad to be able to recognize a scam without calling me."

"I want my grandmother to remain independent."

That's the emotional market.

## 08 — THE PRODUCT

Now—and only now—we can become more explicit about the actual product.

The cinematic experience gives way to a slightly more conventional website structure.

Something like:

Meet Mael.

Then show the actual product interface.

Potentially:

Ask.

Mael helps you understand what something means.

Learn.

Mael remembers the processes you've worked through.

Navigate.

Mael guides you step-by-step.

Verify.

Mael helps you assess suspicious communications.

Stay independent.

Mael helps technology remain something you can use—not something you have to fear.

This is where screenshots, demos, product details, accessibility information, etc. can finally appear.

Because we've already earned the right to explain the product.

## 09 — THE CTA

Potentially:

Technology should meet people where they are.

Then:

Mael is being built to make that possible.

And the CTA could be:

Meet Mael

or, depending on launch status:

Join the journey

Coming soon.

And perhaps the Horizon is visible again in the background.

But now the visitor recognizes it.

That's important.

At the beginning, they didn't know what that golden distortion was.

At the end:

they know.
